# The document schemas and the rule registry are mirrored between this repository and its two
# siblings, and every copy has to be byte-comparable from any checkout. Without this a Windows
# clone stores them with carriage returns, the comparison goes red, and the person who sees it
# reads a line-ending artifact as the mirror having drifted.
*.xsd   text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf

# Scripts are executed, not compared. A shell script stored with carriage returns fails
# on every POSIX system with an error that names the interpreter and not the line ending,
# and a Python tool run from a shebang fails the same way. The agent documentation tells
# an agent to run these by name, so a broken checkout breaks the first instruction.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
